{'symbol': 'ABT', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "The Australian Red Cross Blood Service Selects Abbott's Alinity Solution for Blood and Plasma Screening", 'text': "Abbott announced the Australian Red Cross,Blood Service (Australian Blood Service) has signed a multiple-year agreement for Abbott's most advanced blood and plasma screening technology, Alinity System.  The Australian Blood Service collects 1.5 million donations,each year, providing a safe blood supply to 25 million Australians. The agreement also includes Abbott's total lab automation solution, as well as its informatics and professional services. The Australian Blood Service staff will use AlinIQ AMS (Analyzer Management System), a product of AlinIQ Professional Services, to integrate data from multiple analyzers so staff can view it in one place, providing greater workflow efficiency and better quality control. The Alinity s system will help continuously process up to 600 tests per hour, while the lab automation solution will manage routine, manual tasks so staff can handle up to 3,600 samples per hour."}{'symbol': 'ACN', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Accenture Expands Innovation Hub in Chicago, Adds New Industry X.0 Studio to Accelerate Smart, Connected Products and Services Development for Clients', 'text': 'Accenture has expanded its Chicago Innovation Hub with a new Industry X.0 studio to help clients accelerate the development of new smart connected products and services from months to weeks. The new studio provides a uniquely equipped environment that fuses design, software engineering, hardware engineering and industry expertise. It is located in the mHUB, the nation’s largest and fastest-growing physical product innovation center. Forges are part of Accenture’s Industry X.0 practice, which helps organizations apply advanced digital technologies to reinvent products, services and business models, from design and engineering, to manufacturing and support, to supply chain management and logistics. Accenture currently operates Industry X.0 Forges in Columbus, Ohio; Ann Arbor, Michigan; Des Moines, Iowa; and Jefferson, Iowa. Additional Forges are planned to open across the United States and in Asia in the coming 12 months. The opening of the Forge builds upon Accenture’s continued growth in Chicago. In July 2019, the company announced it will increase the footprint of its Chicago Innovation Hub located in the 500 West Madison building – which was renamed the Accenture Tower – and add 600 highly-skilled tech jobs and significantly grow its apprentice program. The Innovation Hub in Chicago is part of a network of 11 Accenture Innovation Hubs in North America, with other locations in Atlanta; Boston; Columbus, Ohio; metro Detroit; Houston; New York; San Francisco; Seattle; Toronto; and metro Washington, D.C. These hubs are connected to more than 100 Accenture locations around the globe to seamlessly bring the best of the company’s global investments and insights to its clients on the ground in North America.'}{'symbol': 'AES', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The AES Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 09:50 AM', 'text': 'The AES Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 09:50 AM. Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Dante Martins, Cybersecurity Strategy Director.'}{'symbol': 'ALXN', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (NasdaqGS:ALXN) entered into an asset purchase agreement to acquire certain assets of Immune Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (OTCPK:IMNP.Q) for $6 million.', 'text': 'Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (NasdaqGS:ALXN) entered into an asset purchase agreement to acquire certain assets of Immune Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (OTCPK:IMNP.Q) for $6 million on October 21, 2019. The transaction has been approved by the US Bankruptcy Court. On November 25, 2019 the transaction has received all requisite court approvals. The closing of the transaction is expected prior to the end of first quarter of 2020. \n'}{'symbol': 'ALLE', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Allegion plc Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 02:05 PM', 'text': 'Allegion plc Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 02:05 PM. Venue: The TimesCenter, 242 West 41st Street, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Lee Odess, Vice President, Service Provider Market – Americas.'}{'symbol': 'AXP', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Express Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 02:10 PM', 'text': 'American Express Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 02:10 PM. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: David Fabricant, Senior Vice President of Controllership.'}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'McKesson, AmerisourceBergen, Cardinal Health Reach Settlement With Ohio Counties In Opioids Case', 'text': 'DISTRIBUTORS REACH SETTLEMENT WITH OHIO COUNTIES IN OPIOIDS CASE.MCKESSON - CO, AMERISOURCEBERGEN, CARDINAL HEALTH ANNOUNCED THAT THEY HAVE AGREED TO A $215 MILLION SETTLEMENT WITH TWO OHIO COUNTIES.MCKESSON - CO, AMERISOURCEBERGEN, CARDINAL HEALTH "STRONGLY DISPUTE" ALLEGATIONS MADE BY TWO OHIO COUNTIES, CUYAHOGA AND SUMMIT.'}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teva, Mckesson, Cardinal Health, Amerisourcebergen reach opioid settlement for $260 mln - plaintiff lawyer', 'text': 'TEVA PHARMACEUTICAL INDUSTRIES, MCKESSON CORP, CARDINAL HEALTH, AMERISOURCEBERGEN REACH OPIOID SETTLEMENT FOR $260 MILLION - PLAINTIFF LAWYER.'}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-10-21 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'BRIEF- FOUR DRUG COMPANIES REACH LAST-MINUTE SETTLEMENT IN OPIOID LITIGATION - WSJ', 'text': 'Removes extraneous words:.'}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AmerisourceBergen, Cardinal Health and McKesson Reach Settlement with Ohio Counties in Opioids Case', 'text': 'AmerisourceBergen, Cardinal Health and McKesson announced that they have agreed to a $215 million settlement with two Ohio counties, Cuyahoga and Summit, in the first track of the multi-district opioid litigation. With this settlement agreed upon, the companies and the other parties will now continue the work toward a global resolution. While the companies strongly dispute the allegations made by the two counties, they believe settling the bellwether trial is an important stepping stone to achieving a global resolution and delivering meaningful relief. The companies expect settlement funds to be used in support of initiatives to combat the opioid epidemic, including treatment, rehabilitation, mental health and other important efforts.'}{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ANSYS, Inc. Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-24-2019 01:30 PM', 'text': 'ANSYS, Inc. Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-24-2019 01:30 PM. Venue: Double Tree by Hilton San Jose, San Jose, California, United States. Speakers: Gilad Sharon.'}{'symbol': 'ANTM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Anthem, Inc. Presents at 2019 Wolfe Healthcare Conference, Nov-06-2019 08:45 AM', 'text': 'Anthem, Inc. Presents at 2019 Wolfe Healthcare Conference, Nov-06-2019 08:45 AM. Venue: Marriott East Side Hotel, 525 Lexington Avenue at 49th Street, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Felicia Farr Norwood, Executive VP & President of Government Business Division, Jeff Plante, CFO of the Commercial & Specialty Business Division.'}{'symbol': 'T', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "AT&T Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 04:55 PM", 'text': "AT&T Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 04:55 PM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Jason Leiker, AVP, Community Engagement."}{'symbol': 'BAC', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Bank Of America Announces Unlimited Commission-Free Stock, ETF And Options Trading For Preferred Rewards Members', 'text': 'BANK OF AMERICA  - ANNOUNCES UNLIMITED COMMISSION-FREE STOCK, ETF AND OPTIONS TRADING FOR PREFERRED REWARDS MEMBERS.BANK OF AMERICA  - MERRILL EDGE SELF-DIRECTED CLIENTS NOT ENROLLED IN PREFERRED REWARDS TO RECEIVE PRICING OF $2.95 FOR ONLINE STOCK, ETF TRADES.'}{'symbol': 'BDX', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Becton, Dickinson and Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-12-2019 11:20 AM', 'text': 'Becton, Dickinson and Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-12-2019 11:20 AM. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Tom Spoerel, Vice President, Controller and Chief Accounting Officer.'}{'symbol': 'BIIB', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Biogen And Samsung Bioepis To Present Data For Infliximab And Adalimumab Biosimilars At United European Gastroenterology Week', 'text': 'Oct 21  - Biogen Inc <BIIB.O>::BIOGEN AND SAMSUNG BIOEPIS TO PRESENT DATA FOR INFLIXIMAB AND ADALIMUMAB BIOSIMILARS AT UNITED EUROPEAN GASTROENTEROLOGY WEEK.'}{'symbol': 'BLK', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Arcutis, Inc. announced that it has received $94.5 million in funding from a group of investors', 'text': 'On October 21, 2019, Arcutis, Inc. closed the transaction. The company has received $94,500,000 in its series C round of funding from led by new investor HBM Healthcare Investments AG (SWX:HBMN), a fund managed by HBM Partners Ltd. The transaction also included participation from new investors BlackRock, Inc. (NYSE:BLK), Goldman Sachs Group, Merchant Banking Division, Pivotal BioVenture Partners LLC, Omega Fund Management, LLC, and Vivo Capital, LLC and existing investors Bain Capital Life Sciences Fund, L.P., a fund managed by Bain Capital Life Sciences Investors, LLC, Frazier Healthcare Partners, OrbiMed Advisors LLC, and RA Capital Management, LLC. New investors invested more than 50% of investment and rest was contributed by existing investors. Alexander Asam of HBM Partners Ltd. joined company’s board of directors. The company has received more than $160,000,000 in funding date. The company received $94,499,967 from 16 investors pursuant to exemption provided under Regulation D.'}{'symbol': 'CDNS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cadence Design Systems, Inc. Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-22-2019 through Oct-24-2019', 'text': 'Cadence Design Systems, Inc. Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-22-2019 through Oct-24-2019. Venue: Double Tree by Hilton San Jose, San Jose, California, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Oct-22-2019, Bill Acito, Narayanan TV.'}{'symbol': 'CZR', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Caesars Entertainment Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 04:15 PM", 'text': "Caesars Entertainment Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 04:15 PM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Gwen Migita, Global Head of Social Impact, Equity & Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'CPB', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Campbell Soup Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-20-2019 11:55 AM", 'text': "Campbell Soup Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-20-2019 11:55 AM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Megan Maltenfort, Director, Corporate Responsibility & Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'CAH', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'McKesson, AmerisourceBergen, Cardinal Health Reach Settlement With Ohio Counties In Opioids Case', 'text': 'DISTRIBUTORS REACH SETTLEMENT WITH OHIO COUNTIES IN OPIOIDS CASE.MCKESSON - CO, AMERISOURCEBERGEN, CARDINAL HEALTH ANNOUNCED THAT THEY HAVE AGREED TO A $215 MILLION SETTLEMENT WITH TWO OHIO COUNTIES.MCKESSON - CO, AMERISOURCEBERGEN, CARDINAL HEALTH "STRONGLY DISPUTE" ALLEGATIONS MADE BY TWO OHIO COUNTIES, CUYAHOGA AND SUMMIT.'}{'symbol': 'CCL', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Carnival Corporation Launches Remote Global Learning and Development Information System for Employees', 'text': "Carnival Corporation & Plc announced it has launched the Global Learning and Development Information System (GLADIS), providing employees convenient access to the latest technology in training resources for continuous learning and professional development. Part of the company's commitment to achieve and sustain excellence in environmental compliance and overall operations, GLADIS is a single remote learning system capable of operating without internet access to deliver the company's more than\xa0 100,000 shipboard employees a consistent experience, real-time tracking of training requirement completion and greater efficiency in records management and reporting. Developed to ensure shipboard employees have easy access to training resources and to support continuous professional development among shipboard and shoreside employees, the system is now available for crewmembers from the company's nine global cruise line brands as a centralized approach to strengthening the learning culture and lifelong learning process for employees around the world. GLADIS is continuously populated with both brand-specific and corporatewide content, including videos, instructor-led presentations, assessments and podcasts, promoting a greater focus on individual performance, competency mapping and advancement programs through targeted training. Currently, with the shipboard training server installed on all ships in the global fleet, the company remains on track for the full implementation and usage of the training system by the end of 2019. In addition to GLADIS, the company also recently launched CrewTube, a smartphone and tablet application for download featuring video content focused on the onboarding process for new shipboard employees and utilizing the crew's predominant means of communication and information access to help with familiarization, preparation and awareness of life onboard, shipboard operations and Health, Environmental, Safety and Security (HESS) policies prior to joining a ship. Both new remote learning tools were developed by Carnival Corporation to reflect the latest insights in the way information is best processed, including increased digital experiences, accessibility through various devices and small content packages to promote self-learning."}{'symbol': 'CE', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Celanese Corporation Announces Unaudited Consolidated Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Celanese Corporation announced unaudited consolidated earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 1,586 million compared to USD 1,771 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 260 million compared to USD 374 million a year ago. Net income was USD 265 million compared to USD 210 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 2.18 compared to USD 3.02 a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 2.14 compared to USD 2.98 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 2.17 compared to USD 3.00 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 2.13 compared to USD 2.96 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'CNC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Centene Says On Oct. 18, Co's Board Of Directors Authorized Repurchase Of Up To $500 Mln Of Shares", 'text': "Oct 21  - Centene Corp <CNC.N>::CENTENE CORP - ON OCTOBER 18, 2019, CENTENE'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS AUTHORIZED REPURCHASE OF UP TO $500 MILLION OF SHARES OF COMPANY'S COMMON STOCK.CENTENE - NEW REPURCHASE PROGRAM IS IN ADDITION TO PREVIOUSLY APPROVED STOCK REPURCHASE PROGRAM."}{'symbol': 'CRL', 'date': '2019-10-21 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Charles River Laboratories Says Intends To Offer $500 Mln In Senior Notes Due 2028', 'text': 'CHARLES RIVER LABORATORIES - INTENDS TO OFFER $500 MILLION IN AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF SENIOR NOTES DUE 2028.CHARLES RIVER LABORATORIES - INTENDS TO USE NET PROCEEDS OF NOTES OFFERING, CASH TO PREPAY PORTION OF ITS TERM LOAN FACILITY.'}{'symbol': 'CRL', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Charles River Laboratories International, Inc. to Offer $500 Million in Aggregate Principal Amount of Senior Notes Due 2028', 'text': 'Charles River Laboratories International, Inc. announced that it intends to offer $500 million in aggregate principal amount of senior notes due 2028 (the ‘notes’) in an unregistered offering, subject to market conditions. Charles River intends to use the net proceeds of the notes offering and cash on hand to prepay a portion of its term loan facility under its senior credit facilities and to pay related fees and expenses. The notes have not been, and will not be, registered under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended (the “Securities Act”), or under the securities laws of any other jurisdiction. Unless they are registered, the notes may be offered only in transactions that are exempt from registration under the Securities Act and applicable state securities laws. The notes will be offered only to persons reasonably believed to be qualified institutional buyers under Rule 144A under the Securities Act and to non-U.S. persons outside the United States under Regulation S of the Securities Act.'}{'symbol': 'CHTR', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fox And Charter Announce Comprehensive Distribution Agreement', 'text': "FOX CORPORATION AND CHARTER COMMUNICATIONS ANNOUNCE COMPREHENSIVE DISTRIBUTION AGREEMENT.FOX CORP - CO, CHARTER ANNOUNCED LONG-TERM RENEWAL OF THEIR DISTRIBUTION AGREEMENT FOR FOX'S FULL PORTFOLIO OF NEWS, ENTERTAINMENT AND SPORTS NETWORKS.FOX CORP - RENEWAL COVERS DISTRIBUTION OF FOX TELEVISION STATIONS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK, FS1, FS2, BTN, AND FOX DEPORTES.FOX CORP - FOX AND CHARTER WILL COOPERATE TO MITIGATE PIRACY, IMPLEMENTING BUSINESS RULES TO ADDRESS UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO CONTENT."}{'symbol': 'CHTR', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fox Corporation and Charter Communications Announce Comprehensive Distribution Agreement', 'text': "Fox Corporation and Charter Communications, Inc. announced a long-term, comprehensive renewal of their distribution agreement for FOX's full portfolio of leading news, entertainment and sports networks. In addition, FOX and Charter will cooperate to mitigate piracy, implementing business rules to address unauthorized access to content. The renewal covers distribution of the FOX Television Stations, FOX News Channel, FOX Business Network, FS1, FS2, BTN, and FOX Deportes. Additionally, the agreement includes video-on-demand and TV Everywhere rights for those networks, enabling Charter subscribers to watch a wide array of FOX programming live and on-demand through the FOX NOW, FOX Sports and FOX News apps."}{'symbol': 'C', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citi® Supplier Finance Launches with WorldLink® Payment Services', 'text': 'Citi’s Treasury and Trade Solutions (TTS) has launched an enhanced Citi Supplier Finance offering, now with WorldLink® Payment Services (WorldLink), providing clients access to the combined strength of two powerful, industry-recognized platforms. Leveraging one single point of implementation, this virtual interface delivers a streamlined setup and the opportunity for clients to transact across multiple major currencies for settlement. This solution has launched in the U.S. with plans to expand globally.'}{'symbol': 'CFG', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citizens Financial Group, Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $450 million.', 'text': 'Citizens Financial Group, Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $450 million.\n\nSecurity Name: Depositary Shares\nSecurity Type: Depositary Receipt (Preferred Security) (Non Convertible)\nSecurities Offered: 4,534,500\nPrice\\Range: $25\nDiscount Per Security: $0.25\n\nSecurity Name: Depositary Shares\nSecurity Type: Depositary Receipt (Preferred Security) (Non Convertible)\nSecurities Offered: 13,465,500\nPrice\\Range: $25\nDiscount Per Security: $0.7875\n'}{'symbol': 'CMCSA', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Comcast Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 through Nov-01-2019', 'text': 'Comcast Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 through Nov-01-2019. Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Oct-31-2019, Jason Gumbs, Regional Senior Vice President Big South Region, Matthew Summy, Vice President.'}{'symbol': 'CAG', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Utz Quality Foods, LLC completed the acquisition of Direct Store Delivery Snacks Business from Conagra Brands, Inc. (NYSE:CAG).', 'text': "Utz Quality Foods, LLC entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Direct Store Delivery Snacks Business from Conagra Brands, Inc. (NYSE:CAG) for $140 million on September 11, 2019. The purchase price under the agreement is $140 million in expected cash proceeds, subject to final working capital adjustments. The sale includes the Tim's® Cascade Snacks, Hawaiian® Snacks, Erin's®, Snyder® of Berlin and Husman's® brands. The transaction is subject to regulatory approval and customary closing conditions and is expected to be completed before the end of the calendar year. Following the closing of the transaction, the expected annualized impact of the divestiture is a reduction of approximately $110 million of net sales and $0.02 of adjusted EPS. Tim FitzSimons of Jones Day acted as legal advisor to Conagra Brands, Inc\nUtz Quality Foods, LLC completed the acquisition of Direct Store Delivery Snacks Business from Conagra Brands, Inc. (NYSE:CAG) on October 21, 2019. The sale also includes Pop-N-Thin®.\n"}{'symbol': 'CMI', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cummins Inc. Presents at ENG’s 4th Annual Automotive Warranty Management USA Summit, Oct-22-2019 02:30 PM', 'text': 'Cummins Inc. Presents at ENG’s 4th Annual Automotive Warranty Management USA Summit, Oct-22-2019 02:30 PM. Venue: Dearborn, Michigan, United States. Speakers: Graham Swan, Director Global Warranty.'}{'symbol': 'CVS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'CVS Health to Expand Safe Medication Disposal Program in Massachusetts, Giving Customers Drug Disposal Options in All CVS Pharmacy Locations', 'text': "CVS Health announced the expansion of its safe medication disposal program, giving customers access to safer, easier and more convenient drug disposal options at every CVS Pharmacy location in Massachusetts at no cost. As part of its expanded efforts, the company announced the completed installation of 56 safe medication disposal kiosks in select CVS Pharmacy locations in communities across the state, adding to the 43 in-store units previously installed and 43 units donated to local law enforcement. To date, 1,700 CVS Pharmacy locations nationwide have safe medication disposal and the company has donated more than 990 kiosks to law enforcement. These kiosks have collected more than 1.1 million pounds of unwanted or expired medications, including 57,000 pounds in Massachusetts alone. CVS Health also announced that, beginning in 2020, all CVS Pharmacy locations that don't currently offer a safe medication disposal kiosk will now offer DisposeRx, a simple solution that enables customers to safely discard their unwanted or expired medications at home. New and existing patients filling prescriptions can request a free DisposeRx packet and opioid safety information brochure when picking up their prescription at any time. DisposeRx packets, according to the manufacturer, contain proprietary solidifying materials that make safe disposal of unused medication simple. When water and the DisposeRx powder are added to unwanted medications in the prescription vial and shaken, the drugs are rendered unusable, allowing for safe disposal at home. CVS Health unveiled its safe medication disposal expansion plans, including a commitment to install an additional 1,000 drug disposal kiosks in select CVS Pharmacy locations across the country and donate up to 400 units to law enforcement in 2020, during an event inside a CVS Pharmacy location in Boston with Senator William Brownsberger, and State Representatives Jon Santiago and Dan Cullinane, and community health organizations."}{'symbol': 'DHR', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sartorius Aktiengesellschaft (XTRA:SRT) signed an agreement to acquire certain businesses\xa0from Danaher Corporation (NYSE:DHR) for approximately $750 million.', 'text': "Sartorius Aktiengesellschaft (XTRA:SRT) signed an agreement to acquire certain businesses\xa0from Danaher Corporation (NYSE:DHR) for approximately $750 million on October 18, 2019. The consideration will be paid in cash. The business consists of label-free biomolecular characterization, chromatography hardware and resins, and microcarriers and particle validation standards businesses. The label-free biomolecular characterization business will become part of Sartorius’ bioanalytics unit within its Lab Products & Services division. The chromatography hardware and resins business will be part of Bioprocess Solutions division. BNP Paribas is financing the transaction, acting as sole lead arranger, bookrunner and underwriter. The business reported revenues of approximately $140 million in 2018.\n\nDanaher entered into the agreement to\xa0sell\xa0these businesses as a step towards obtaining regulatory approval for its pending\xa0acquisition\xa0of the Biopharma business of General Electric Company (NYSE:GE). The closing of this transaction is conditioned upon Danaher's closing its\xa0acquisition\xa0of the GE Biopharma business. The transaction is also subject to customary closing conditions, antitrust clearance and approvals from various regulatory authorities. The transaction is expected to close\xa0in the first quarter of 2020.\n\nMichael P. Brueck, James Jian Hu, Francisco J. Morales Barrón and Daniel E. Wolf of Kirkland & Ellis LLP acted as legal advisors for Danaher. Michael Bernhardt, Roland Hlawaty, Scott Golenbock, Christoph Rothenfusser, Alexander Rinne and Fiona Schaeffer of Milbank LLP acted as legal advisor to Sartorius Aktiengesellschaft (XTRA:SRT) in the transaction. Johannes Tieves of Hengeler Mueller advised BNP Paribas on financing of the transaction.\n"}{'symbol': 'DAL', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $896.427 million.', 'text': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $896.427 million.\n\nSecurity Name: 2.9% Senior Unsubordinated Unsecured Notes due October 28, 2024\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: $900 million\nPrice\\Range: 99.603%\nDiscount Per Security: 0.6%\nSecurity Features: Callable\nCoupon Type: Fixed\n'}{'symbol': 'D', 'date': '2019-10-21 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dominion Energy Announces Equity Recapitalization of Cove Point', 'text': 'DOMINION ENERGY ANNOUNCES EQUITY RECAPITALIZATION OF COVE POINT.DOMINION ENERGY INC - AGREEMENT WITH BROOKFIELD SUPER-CORE INFRASTRUCTURE PARTNERS.DOMINION ENERGY INC - COMPANY WILL TRANSFER A 25 PERCENT NON-CONTROLLING EQUITY INTEREST IN COVE POINT TO BROOKFIELD.DOMINION ENERGY INC - DEAL FOR CASH CONSIDERATION OF JUST OVER $2 BILLION, EXCLUDING WORKING CAPITAL.'}{'symbol': 'D', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Brookfield Super-Core Infrastructure Partners L.P. managed by Brookfield Asset Management Inc. (TSX:BAM.A) (Brookfield) entered into an recapitalization agreement to acquire 25% stake in Dominion Energy Cove Point LNG, LP from Dominion Energy, Inc. (NYSE:D) for approximately $2 billion.', 'text': "Brookfield Super-Core Infrastructure Partners L.P. managed by Brookfield Asset Management Inc. (TSX:BAM.A) (Brookfield) entered into an recapitalization agreement to acquire 25% stake in Dominion Energy Cove Point LNG, LP from Dominion Energy, Inc. (NYSE:D) for approximately $2 billion on October 21, 2019. Brookfield will make the payment in cash which excludes working capital. The transaction is expected to be completed by the end of 2019. The proceeds are expected to be used for general corporate purposes including significantly reducing the annual common equity financing described at the Dominion's investor day in March 2019. Jay Horine, David Harkin, Andrew Castaldo, Alex Berezner, Jared Hendrick and Eric Anderson of J.P. Morgan acted as the financial advisors and Joanne Katsantonis, Jay Hughes and Colin Bumby of McGuireWoods LLP acted as the legal advisors to Dominion Energy. Doug Bacon, Allan Kirk, Roald Nashi, Rustin Brown, Brian Greene, Brooksany Barrowes, Nic Gladd, David Wheat and Alexandra Farmer of Kirkland & Ellis LLP acted as the legal advisors to Brookfield.\n"}{'symbol': 'ETSY', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Etsy, Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 01:30 PM", 'text': "Etsy, Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-18-2019 01:30 PM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Hilary Young, Senior Sustainability Manager."}{'symbol': 'ES', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eversource Energy, Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 06, 2019', 'text': 'Eversource Energy, Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 06, 2019'}{'symbol': 'FB', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Facebook To Update List Of State-Controlled Media On Rolling Basis Starting Nov', 'text': 'Oct 21  - Facebook Inc <FB.O>::FACEBOOK - REMOVED 4 SEPARATE NETWORKS OF ACCOUNTS, PAGES & GROUPS ON FACEBOOK & INSTAGRAM FOR ENGAGING IN "COORDINATED INAUTHENTIC BEHAVIOR".FACEBOOK INC - WILL UPDATE LIST OF STATE-CONTROLLED MEDIA ON A ROLLING BASIS BEGINNING IN NOVEMBER.FACEBOOK SAYS LAUNCHING FACEBOOK PROTECT TO FURTHER SECURE ACCOUNTS OF ELECTED OFFICIALS & CANDIDATES WHO MAY BE VULNERABLE TO TARGETING BY HACKERS.FACEBOOK INC -  UPDATING AD LIBRARY, AD LIBRARY REPORT & AD LIBRARY API.FACEBOOK INC - BEGINNING MONDAY, PAGE ADMINS CAN ENROLL THEIR ORGANIZATION’S FACEBOOK AND INSTAGRAM ACCOUNTS IN FACEBOOK PROTECT.FACEBOOK INC -  UPDATING AD LIBRARY TO INCLUDE A NEW U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE SPEND TRACKER.FACEBOOK INC -  ADDING USEFUL API FILTERS, PROVIDING PROGRAMMATIC ACCESS TO DOWNLOAD AD CREATIVES.FACEBOOK SAYS ADDING MORE INFORMATION ABOUT WHO IS BEHIND A PAGE ON FACEBOOK.FACEBOOK - INTRODUCING NEW POP-UP THAT WILL APPEAR WHEN SHARING POSTS ON INSTAGRAM THAT INCLUDE CONTENT DEBUNKED BY THIRD-PARTY FACT-CHECKERS.FACEBOOK INC - PARTICIPANTS IN FACEBOOK PROTECT WILL BE REQUIRED TO TURN ON 2-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION.FACEBOOK INC - HAVE NOW IMPLEMENTED POLICY BANNING PAID ADVERTISING THAT SUGGESTS VOTING IS USELESS OR MEANINGLESS, OR ADVISES PEOPLE NOT TO VOTE.FACEBOOK - OVER NEXT MONTH, CONTENT RATED "FALSE OR PARTLY FALSE" BY 3RD PARTY FACT-CHECKER TO BE MORE PROMINENTLY LABELED ON FACEBOOK, INSTAGRAM.'}{'symbol': 'FDX', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'FedEx Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019', 'text': 'FedEx Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 . Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Dale Chrystie.'}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ford Motor Company Presents at ENG’s 4th Annual Automotive Warranty Management USA Summit, Oct-22-2019 through Oct-23-2019', 'text': 'Ford Motor Company Presents at ENG’s 4th Annual Automotive Warranty Management USA Summit, Oct-22-2019 through Oct-23-2019. Venue: Dearborn, Michigan, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Oct-22-2019, Sharita Crawford, Global Warranty Policy, Training & Field Operations Manager.'}{'symbol': 'FOXA', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fox And Charter Announce Comprehensive Distribution Agreement', 'text': "FOX CORPORATION AND CHARTER COMMUNICATIONS ANNOUNCE COMPREHENSIVE DISTRIBUTION AGREEMENT.FOX CORP - CO, CHARTER ANNOUNCED LONG-TERM RENEWAL OF THEIR DISTRIBUTION AGREEMENT FOR FOX'S FULL PORTFOLIO OF NEWS, ENTERTAINMENT AND SPORTS NETWORKS.FOX CORP - RENEWAL COVERS DISTRIBUTION OF FOX TELEVISION STATIONS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK, FS1, FS2, BTN, AND FOX DEPORTES.FOX CORP - FOX AND CHARTER WILL COOPERATE TO MITIGATE PIRACY, IMPLEMENTING BUSINESS RULES TO ADDRESS UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO CONTENT."}{'symbol': 'FOXA', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fox Corporation Names Yoel Flohr Executive Vice President of Technology & Digital', 'text': 'Fox Corporation announced the appointment of Yoel Flohr as Executive Vice President of Technology & Digital. Flohr, who will report to Fox Corporation Chief Technology Officer and President of Digital Paul Cheesbrough, will lead the digital product portfolio for FOX Entertainment. In this role Flohr will oversee existing digital products and relationships, including FOX Now, and will work closely with the FOX Entertainment team to develop and grow new digital businesses, partnerships and revenues. Flohr previously served as Executive Vice President of Digital and Franchise Development for AMC Networks and Studios, where he oversaw its digital business. Before joining AMC in 2016, Flohr co-founded Thirty Labs Inc., a start-up studio focused on the emerging digital video space, and earlier founded Ventuation, a strategic consulting and digital incubation firm. Prior to this, Flohr was the Vice President of Digital at Shine Group.'}{'symbol': 'FCX', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Freeport-McMoRan Inc. Announces Appointment of John J. Stephens to its Board of Directors and as a Member of the Audit Committee of the Board of Directors', 'text': 'Freeport-McMoRan Inc. announced the appointment of John J. Stephens to its Board of Directors and as a member of the Audit Committee of the Board of Directors. Mr. Stephens has served as Senior Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of AT&T Inc., since 2011. He has responsibility for financial planning, corporate development, accounting, tax, auditing, treasury, investor relations and corporate real estate. Prior to his current position, Stephens held a series of successive positions in the finance department.'}{'symbol': 'GE', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'GE Hitachi Nuclear Energy Announces Small Modular Reactor Technology Collaboration In Poland', 'text': 'Oct 21  - General Electric Co <GE.N>::GE - GE HITACHI NUCLEAR ENERGY ANNOUNCES SMALL MODULAR REACTOR TECHNOLOGY COLLABORATION IN POLAND.GE - GE HITACHI NUCLEAR ENERGY, SYNTHOS SA TO COLLABORATE ON POTENTIAL DEPLOYMENT APPLICATIONS FOR GEH’S BWRX-300 SMALL MODULAR REACTOR IN POLAND.'}{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "General Motors Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-19-2019 01:30 PM", 'text': "General Motors Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-19-2019 01:30 PM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Sharon Basel, Senior Manager, Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gilead Sciences, Inc. Presents at BioNetwork Partnering Summit, Oct-24-2019 04:15 PM', 'text': 'Gilead Sciences, Inc. Presents at BioNetwork Partnering Summit, Oct-24-2019 04:15 PM. Venue: The Ritz-Carlton Laguna Niguel, Laguna Niguel, California, United States. Speakers: Monica Viziano, Executive Director, Alliance Management.'}{'symbol': 'GS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': '\u200dClearwater Launches New Platform With Goldman Sachs for Liquidity Management', 'text': 'Oct 21  - \u200dclearwater::\u200dCLEARWATER - ANNOUNCED LAUNCH OF A NEW PLATFORM CONNECTION IN PARTNERSHIP WITH GOLDMAN SACHS & CO. LLC AND GOLDMAN SACHS ASSET MANAGEMENT\u200b.'}{'symbol': 'HAL', 'date': '2019-10-21 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Halliburton Executive Says Co To Continue Cutting Cost in N. America - Conference Call', 'text': 'HALLIBURTON SAYS FOR 2020, SEE MORE INTERNATIONAL TOP LINE, MARGIN GROWTH OPPORTUNITIES COMING FOR MATURE FIELDS AND SHALLOW WATER MARKETS - CONF CALL.HALLIBURTON SAYS STACKED MORE EQUIPMENT IN Q3 THAN FIRST SIX MONTHS OF THE YEAR.HALLIBURTON SAYS "WILL KEEP REDUCING COST IN OUR NORTH AMERICAN OPERATIONS" AFTER RECENT JOB CUTS.HALLIBURTON SAYS FOR Q4, SEES CUSTOMER ACTIVITY TO DECLINE ACROSS ALL BASINS IN NORTH AMERICA LAND, IMPACTING BOTH DRILLING AND COMPLETION BUSINESS.HALLIBURTON SAYS FOR Q4, FEEDBACK FROM CUSTOMERS LEAD CO TO BELIEVE RIG COUNT, COMPLETIONS ACTIVITY MAYBE LOWER THAN IN Q4 LAST YEAR.HALLIBURTON, AFTER RECENT JOB CUTS, SAYS IN Q4 PLAN TO UNDERTAKE FURTHER COST REDUCTIONS BY STREAMLINING OPERATIONS AND CORPORATE FUNCTIONS.HALLIBURTON SAYS WATCHING TREND OF DECELERATION OF INCREMENTAL U.S. PRODUCTION GROWTH BROUGHT ABOUT BY CAPITAL DISCIPLINE.HALLIBURTON SAYS RECORD-BREAKING 2018 PRODUCTION GROWTH WILL NOT BE REPLICATED IN 2019.HALLIBURTON SAYS CURRENT PROJECTIONS FOR 2020 INDICATE A FURTHER DECLINE IN PRODUCTION FROM THE CURRENT YEAR ESTIMATES.HALLIBURTON SAYS EXPECT EQUIPMENT ATTRITION TO CONTINUE INTO 2020.HALLIBURTON CO - 2019 CAPEX GUIDANCE REMAINS UNCHANGED.HALLIBURTON- IN Q4, FOR DRILLING & EVALUATION, SEE SEQUENTIAL REVENUE TO BE FLAT TO UP LOW SINGLE DIGITS, WITH MARGIN IMPROVEMENT OF 425-475 BASIS POINTS.'}{'symbol': 'HAL', 'date': '2019-10-21 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Halliburton Reports Q3 EPS Of $0.34', 'text': 'HALLIBURTON ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.QTRLY REPORTED NET INCOME OF $0.34 PER DILUTED SHARE.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE $5,550 MILLION VERSUS $6,172 MILLION.QTRLY COMPLETION AND PRODUCTION REVENUE $3,506 MILLION VERSUS $4,170 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.34, REVENUE VIEW $5.81 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.HALLIBURTON-QTRLY NORTH AMERICA REVENUE WAS DOWN 11% VERSUS Q2 PRIMARILY RELATED TO LOWER ACTIVITY & PRICING IN PRESSURE PUMPING & WELL CONSTRUCTION SERVICES.REMAIN CONFIDENT THAT CO WILL ACHIEVE HIGH SINGLE-DIGIT INTERNATIONAL GROWTH FOR ALL OF 2019.QTRLY DRILLING AND EVALUATION REVENUE $2,044 MILLION VERSUS $2,002 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'HAL', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Halliburton Company Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Halliburton Company announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 5,550 million compared to USD 6,172 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 536 million compared to USD 716 million a year ago. Net income was USD 295 million compared to USD 435 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.34 compared to USD 0.5 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 17,217 million compared to USD 18,059 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 1,204 million compared to USD 1,859 million a year ago. Net income was USD 522 million compared to USD 992 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.6 compared to USD 1.13 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'HSIC', 'date': '2019-10-21 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Henry Schein- Henry Schein To Be Dismissed From Summit County Opioid Litigation', 'text': "HENRY SCHEIN INC - HENRY SCHEIN TO BE DISMISSED FROM SUMMIT COUNTY OPIOID LITIGATION.HENRY SCHEIN INC - PLAINTIFF HAS AGREED TO DISMISS COMPANY WITH PREJUDICE AS A DEFENDANT IN OPIOID LITIGATION INVOLVING SUMMIT COUNTY, OHIO.HENRY SCHEIN INC - WILL PAY $250,000 OF SUMMIT COUNTY'S EXPENSES.HENRY SCHEIN INC - TO MAKE DONATION TO ESTABLISH PAIN MANAGEMENT EDUCATION FOUNDATION."}{'symbol': 'HSIC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Henry Schein to Be Dismissed from Summit County Opioid Litigation', 'text': 'Henry Schein, Inc. announced that the plaintiff has agreed to dismiss the company with prejudice as a defendant in the opioid litigation involving Summit County, Ohio, presently before the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of Ohio. Henry Schein, working with Summit County, will make the donation to a Pain Management Education Foundation dedicated to making grants supporting and aggregating research around best practices for pain management, including the prescription of opioids and alternatives, and educating dentists and physicians, clinical associates, patients, and patient networks on those best practices along with the risks of opioid addiction and alternative pain management treatment options for key indications. Henry Schein will pay $250,000 of Summit County’s expenses.'}{'symbol': 'HSY', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "The Hershey Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-19-2019 01:30 PM", 'text': "The Hershey Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-19-2019 01:30 PM. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Speakers: Carly Greenberg, Environmental Sustainability & ESG Reporting."}{'symbol': 'HPE', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Hewlett Packard Enterprise Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019", 'text': "Hewlett Packard Enterprise Company Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-18-2019, John Frey, Senior Technologist and Strategist, IT Efficiency and Sustainability. Nov-19-2019, John Frey, Senior Technologist and Strategist, IT Efficiency and Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'HON', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Honeywell Unveils Micro Power Unit for Business Jet Segment', 'text': "The company famous for inventing the auxiliary power unit (APU) for passenger airplanes has unveiled a similar product for the turboprop and light jet segment aimed at upending the way these aircraft deliver on-ground power. Honeywell's Micro Power Units for business and private airplanes, helicopters, and advanced ground vehicles deliver many of the same benefits of APUs. These include major savings from reduced fuel burn, coupled with mobile power on the ground for critical aircraft systems such as air conditioning and avionics. Honeywell's Micro Power Unit, or mPU, gives aircraft owners and operators a new and smarter way to provide power autonomously in any ground environment. This drastically decreases fuel burn while increasing overall aircraft efficiency and hull value. The mPU is compact enough to fit in aircraft that have space limitations while still providing enough power to operate air conditioning, charge batteries, conduct flight planning and assist main engine start without using additional power sources. When compared with using the main engines to power aircraft systems, the mPU can result in an 80% reduction in fuel burn while on the ground. The mPU also avoids the hassle of securing costly or simply unavailable ground power — particularly in remote locations. The mPU adds value to aircraft by introducing a new, low-cost and mobile power source for ground operations. Thanks to its efficient design, it also removes the need to use the main engines to access basic aircraft functions. This can help unlock new routes to more remote areas where power is not readily available, greatly increasing an aircraft's overall utility. The mPU can also offer similar solutions to military ground vehicles. The fuel-efficient, lightweight power source allows armored vehicles to access power without running its main engines. The mPU offers a low-noise and low-emissions solution to provide power for electronics and cooling during silent watch and other critical missions."}{'symbol': 'HUM', 'date': '2019-10-21 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Humana And Microsoft Announce Multiyear Strategic Partnership', 'text': 'HUMANA AND MICROSOFT ANNOUNCE MULTIYEAR STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP TO REIMAGINE HEALTH FOR AGING POPULATIONS AND THEIR CARE TEAMS.MICROSOFT CORP - AS PART OF STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP WITH HUMANA, COS COMMITTED TO MULTIYEAR RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT INVESTMENT.'}{'symbol': 'INFO', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IHS Markit Ltd. Announces Board Changes', 'text': 'IHS Markit announced the appointment of Deborah Orida as an independent director to its board and the retirement of Richard Roedel from the board. Ms. Orida’s appointment increases the size of the IHS Markit board to 12 directors. Ms. Orida will also serve on the Human Resources committee of the board. Ms. Orida is Senior Managing Director & Global Head of Active Equities at Canada Pension Plan Investment Board (CPPIB). She joined CPPIB in 2009 and has held senior leadership roles, including Managing Director, Head of Relationship Investments International, where she covered Europe and Asia. Most recently she was Managing Director and Head of Private Equity Asia, based in Hong Kong. Prior to joining CPPIB, Ms. Orida spent nine years at Goldman Sachs in New York and Toronto. Richard Roedel has decided not to seek re-election to the board when his current term expires at the annual general meeting of shareholders in April 2020. Roedel, a former chair and CEO of BDO Seidman LLP, has served on the IHS Markit board for 15 years.'}{'symbol': 'INTC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Corning Announces 5G In-Building Network Collaboration with Intel', 'text': 'Corning Incorporated and Intel announced a strategic collaboration to accelerate the availability of 5G in buildings. The two companies will work together to deliver a virtual platform for Corning’s 5G network solutions powered by Intel Xeon Scalable processors and Intel FlexRAN Reference Software Architecture. This co-innovation effort will create a streamlined path for mobile network operators and enterprise building owners to deploy 5G solutions that meet the performance demands of their customers and enable faster adoption of 5G applications, with the ability to scale from small to large venues and enterprises. The collaboration combines Corning’s wireless connectivity portfolio and Intel’s technologies, including second-generation Intel Xeon Scalable processors, Intel FlexRAN 5G and 4G Reference Software, Intel FPGA Programmable Acceleration Card N3000, and 10/25/40Gb Intel Ethernet 700 Series Network Adapters to support 5G innovation as deployments proliferate around the world.'}{'symbol': 'IBM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'International Business Machines Corporation Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 05:30 PM', 'text': 'International Business Machines Corporation Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 05:30 PM. Venue: The TimesCenter, 242 West 41st Street, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Lisa Seacat DeLuca, Director Digital IoT Transformation & Digital Twin, Distinguished Engineer, Project Whitespace Founder.'}{'symbol': 'IVZ', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Invesco Releases Findings from Fourth Annual Global Factor Investing Study, the Largest of Its Kind', 'text': "Invesco released findings from its fourth annual Global Factor Investing Study, the largest of its kind. This year's study focuses on the key questions facing investors of varying levels of factor adoption, including challenges and preferences. This year, the study found that respondents have continued to increase factor allocations overall; both in the number of factors they target and their usage of multi-factor strategies. Nearly half (45%) of the investors surveyed globally increased factor allocations in the last year, and 65% of investors in North America intend to increase their factor allocations over the next three years. Also, in 2019 over 66% of respondents have also reported that their factor investing performance met or exceeded expectations the performance of their traditional active or market-weighted allocations. Investors are also maintaining their conviction in factor investing with 77% of respondents in North America waiting at least three years before judging performance. Invesco also reveals that investors, in aggregate, are 1) more widely interested in factor fixed income strategies and have opinions on which factors should work best, 2) moving to a more dynamic approach for implementation of factors by a three-to-one majority, 3) taking more defensive, long-term factor positions. Since last year's Global Factor Study, there has been a notable increase in the proportion of North American respondents who believe factor investing can be extended to fixed income. Invesco found that 61% of institutional investors and 76% of wealth managers now view the approach as being applicable. The growing belief is tied to widespread recognition that the returns of all fixed-income portfolios, whether they are built utilizing a factor-based approach or not, will be implicitly driven by exposure to factors.Of the potential factors identifiable within fixed income, belief in a yield/carry factor is the most prevalent, with 64% of respondents identifying it as the top factor, which may explain the increase to such strategies over the past 12 months. Additional factors to be explored in fixed income, yield/carry was followed by liquidity, value and quality (54%, 46% and 42% respectively). Bond market inefficiencies, coupled with a near four-decade bull-market run, have helped to support the case for active management within fixed income. Factor investing in fixed income includes many of the benefits that have driven the strong performance of active fixed-income strategies, while also offering transparency and a potentially attractive cost."}{'symbol': 'IRM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Iron Mountain Announces Rooftop Solar Installation of Any Data Center in the US', 'text': "Iron Mountain Incorporated\xa0announced that they have closed on their largest on-site solar power-purchase agreement (PPA) contract to date. The 7.2 MW-rated solar installation at Iron Mountain's data center in Edison, New Jersey (NJE-1) is forecast to generate more than 9 Million KWhrs per year, which is enough electricity to power more than 1,000 homes for a year. The solar installation will provide approximately 15% of the data center's current energy load. Developed in collaboration with a subsidiary of NextEra Energy Resources, a leading clean energy company with approximately 21,000 MW of net generating capacity, and Black Bear Energy, which facilitated the project acting as the owner's representative to Iron Mountain, the project is slated for completion at the end of 2019. It will be the largest rooftop solar installation of any data center in the USA. In collaboration with Renewable Energy Buyers Alliance (REBA) and Business for Social Responsibility (BSR), Iron Mountain participated in the Future of Internet Power (FoIP) effort to develop an industry supported open source protocol that enables data center customers to claim the benefits of renewable energy contracts. Iron Mountain's Green Power Pass, launched in February of this year, is the first generally available solution for the data center industry that meets the full transparency and auditability requirements of the FoIP protocol.\xa0 Green Power Pass enables Iron Mountain data center customers to report carbon emission reductions associated with the green power consumed at any Iron Mountain data center worldwide. Early adopters of the Green Power Pass include Akamai, WeWork and Arizona State University."}{'symbol': 'JNJ', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Johnson & Johnson Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019', 'text': 'Johnson & Johnson Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 . Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: JOSEPH HORNER, Lead Data Scientist, Supply Chain Digital & Analytics.'}{'symbol': 'JCI', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Johnson Controls International plc, Q4 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019', 'text': 'Johnson Controls International plc, Q4 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019'}{'symbol': 'JPM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'S&P Dow Jones Indices LLC, Eyes on Asia  Restocking the Investment Toolkit, Oct 24, 2019', 'text': 'S&P Dow Jones Indices LLC, Eyes on Asia  Restocking The Investment Toolkit, Oct 24, 2019. Venue: Cuisine Cuisine, IFC, Hong Kong, Hong Kong.'}{'symbol': 'K', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kellogg Company Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019', 'text': 'Kellogg Company Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 . Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Genaro Cardenas, Director IT Digital Supply Chain.'}{'symbol': 'KEY', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'KeyCorp Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-06-2019 11:20 AM', 'text': 'KeyCorp Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-06-2019 11:20 AM. Venue: The St. Regis Hotel, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Donald R. Kimble, Vice Chairman & CFO.'}{'symbol': 'LH', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'HealthEC, LabCorp, and the New Jersey Primary Care Association Announce Strategic Collaboration to Advance Value-Based Care at Community Health Centers', 'text': 'LabCorp, HealthEC, LLC and the New Jersey Primary Care Association (NJPCA) announced the development of a database and information exchange platform supporting participating NJPCA health centers. The project will help NJPCA members achieve value-based care objectives by providing integrated lab and clinical data in a more accessible, comprehensive and secure manner, with a focus on improving outcomes for patients with chronic conditions, such as diabetes and chronic kidney disease. The platform will be available through LabCorp’s Care Intelligence application, which is supported by HealthEC. It will allow for population health analyses, showing trends across communities, and for enhanced monitoring of individual patients to understand when intervention is needed and how a patient is responding to treatment.'}{'symbol': 'LDOS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Leidos Adds Automation Anywhere and Tanium to its Partner Network', 'text': 'Leidos announced the addition of Automation Anywhere and Tanium into the Emerging Technology category of the Leidos Alliance Partner Network. This category includes start-ups or companies that have a capability that either improves upon an existing technology or is entirely new. Leidos focuses on connecting the right companies to help cultivate the right technological solutions for customers. Some of the key attributes the company considers when adding new suppliers include: innovative products; joint independent research and development opportunities; technical roadmap awareness; and extensive training opportunities.'}{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eli Lilly and Company Declares Fourth-Quarter 2019 Dividend, Payable on December 10, 2019', 'text': 'The board of directors of Eli Lilly and Company has declared a dividend for the fourth quarter of 2019 of $0.645 per share on outstanding common stock. The dividend is payable December 10, 2019, to shareholders of record at the close of business on November 15, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'LYV', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Live Nation Acquires David Grutman's Groot Hospitality", 'text': "LIVE NATION ACQUIRES DAVID GRUTMAN'S GROOT HOSPITALITY.LIVE NATION ENTERTAINMENT INC - DAVID GRUTMAN WILL REMAIN AS CEO OF GROOT HOSPITALITY ALONG WITH EXECUTIVES CHRIS CUOMO AND MO GARCIA.LIVE NATION ENTERTAINMENT INC - HAS ACQUIRED A MAJORITY STAKE IN DAVID GRUTMAN'S GROOT HOSPITALITY."}{'symbol': 'LYV', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. (NYSE:LYV) acquired a majority stake in Groot Hospitality LLC.', 'text': 'Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. (NYSE:LYV) acquired a majority stake in Groot Hospitality LLC on October 21, 2019. Pursuant to the transaction, David Grutman will remain as Chief Executive Officer of Groot Hospitality along with executives Chris Cuomo and Mo Garcia. Augusto Sasso, Ramy Ibrahim and Jeremy Burke of Moelis & Company (NYSE:MC) acted as financial advisors; Branch Furtado of Grubman Shire Meiselas & Sacks PC and, Iryna Ivashchuk and Mitchell Goldberg of Berger Singerman LLP acted as legal advisors to Groot Hospitality.\nLive Nation Entertainment, Inc. (NYSE:LYV) completed the acquisition of a majority stake in Groot Hospitality LLC on October 21, 2019. \n'}{'symbol': 'LMT', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lockheed Martin Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019', 'text': 'Lockheed Martin Corporation Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 . Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Don Kinard, Senior Fellow.'}{'symbol': 'MA', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mastercard Incorporated Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 03:40 PM', 'text': 'Mastercard Incorporated Presents at IoTC NEXT: The Connected Future Summit, Nov-12-2019 03:40 PM. Venue: The TimesCenter, 242 West 41st Street, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Stephane Wyper, SVP for New Commerce Partnerships.'}{'symbol': 'MDT', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sean Salmon Named Executive Vice President and Group President of Medtronic Diabetes', 'text': "Medtronic plc announced that Sean Salmon, previously Senior Vice President (SVP) and President, Coronary and Structural Heart (CSH) within the Cardiac and Vascular Group of Medtronic, has been named Executive Vice President (EVP) and Group President of Medtronic Diabetes, effective today. Salmon will serve on the company's Executive Committee and succeeds Hooman Hakami, who is leaving Medtronic. To ensure a seamless transition, Hakami will remain an advisor to executive leadership on an as needed basis through February 2020."}{'symbol': 'MRK', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Merck & Co., Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 04:20 PM', 'text': 'Merck & Co., Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 04:20 PM. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Rita A. Karachun, Senior VP of Finance & Global Controller.'}{'symbol': 'MSFT', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Microsoft Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019", 'text': "Microsoft Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-18-2019, Jim Hanna, Director, Datacenter Community Development. Nov-19-2019, Josh Henretig, Senior Director, AI for Earth & Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'MSI', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Motorola to Launch Foldable Razr 2019 Smartphone', 'text': "Motorola announced that it might launch its foldable Razr 2019 smartphone on November 13, 2019. A GIF integrated into Motorola's media invite, which showcases a phone being folded and unfolded. Thus hinting at the launch of Motorola Razr 2019."}{'symbol': 'MSCI', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'MSCI Inc. Presents at RI New York 2019 - Sustainable Business and Finance, Dec-04-2019', 'text': 'MSCI Inc. Presents at RI New York 2019 - Sustainable Business and Finance, Dec-04-2019 . Venue: 117 West 46th Street, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Ric Marshall, Executive Director, ESG Research team.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'NASDAQ Vice Chairman Bruce E. Aust To Retire', 'text': 'NASDAQ VICE CHAIRMAN BRUCE E. AUST TO RETIRE.NASDAQ INC - BRUCE AUST WILL RETIRE AS VICE CHAIRMAN AT END OF 2019.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Nasdaq, Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019", 'text': "Nasdaq, Inc. Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-19-2019, Evan Harvey, Global Head of Sustainability. Nov-20-2019, Evan Harvey, Global Head of Sustainability."}{'symbol': 'NFLX', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Netflix Announces Proposed $2.0 Billion Offering Of Senior Notes', 'text': 'NETFLIX ANNOUNCES PROPOSED $2.0 BILLION OFFERING OF SENIOR NOTES.NETFLIX - INTENDS TO USE NET PROCEEDS FOR GENERAL CORPORATE PURPOSES, WHICH MAY INCLUDE CONTENT ACQUISITIONS, PRODUCTION AND DEVELOPMENT, OTHERS.NETFLIX - INTENDS TO OFFER ABOUT $2.0 BILLION OF U.S. DOLLAR DENOMINATED AND EURO DENOMINATED SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES IN TWO SERIES.'}{'symbol': 'NFLX', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Netflix Announces Proposed Offering of Senior Notes', 'text': 'Netflix, Inc. announced that it intends to offer, subject to market and other considerations, approximately $2.0 billion aggregate principal amount of U.S. dollar denominated and euro denominated senior unsecured notes in two series through an offering to persons reasonably believed to be qualified institutional buyers pursuant to Rule 144A under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, and outside the United States to non-U.S. persons pursuant to Regulation S under the Securities Act. The interest rate, redemption provisions, maturity date and other terms of each series of Notes will be determined by negotiations between Netflix and the initial purchasers.'}{'symbol': 'NEM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Newmont Goldcorp Corporation Announces Executive Changes', 'text': 'Newmont Goldcorp Corporation has appointed Dan Janney to continue improving the Company’s safety and operational performance in North America. Most recently, Mr. Janney was serving as Newmont Goldcorp’s Group Executive supporting the Full Potential continuous improvement work in the region. He will assume the full accountabilities of the Regional Senior Vice President role in North America, effective October 21, 2019. Mr. Janney succeeds Todd White who has served in the role since closing of the Newmont Goldcorp transaction in April. Mr. Janney will report directly to Rob Atkinson, Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer. Mr. Janney joined Newmont in May of 2017 as the General Manager for Integration and Optimization for North America and, in February of 2019, he was appointed General Manager Operations Services for North America. Prior to joining Newmont, Mr. Janney was a Technical Consultant with Alacer Gold Corp. based in Turkey.'}{'symbol': 'NOC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Northrop Grumman Corporation Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-22-2019 11:30 AM', 'text': 'Northrop Grumman Corporation Presents at 16th Annual International Wafer-Level Packaging Conference, Oct-22-2019 11:30 AM. Venue: Double Tree by Hilton San Jose, San Jose, California, United States. Speakers: Samuel Massa.'}{'symbol': 'NVDA', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'New NVIDIA EGX Edge Supercomputing Platform Accelerates AI, IoT, 5G at the Edge', 'text': 'NVIDIA announced the NVIDIA EGX Edge Supercomputing Platform, a high-performance, cloud-native platform that lets organizations harness rapidly streaming data from factory floors, manufacturing inspection lines and city streets to securely deliver next-generation AI, IoT and 5G-based services at scale, with low latency. The EGX platform features software to support a wide range of applications, including NVIDIA Metropolis, which can be used to build smart cities and intelligent video analytics applications, as well as the just-announced NVIDIA Aerial™ software developer kit [5]. Aerial allows telcos to build completely virtualized 5G radio access networks that are highly programmable, scalable and energy efficient, and can ultimately enable them to offer new services such as smart factories, AR/VR and cloud gaming.'}{'symbol': 'NXPI', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'NXP Semiconductors N.V. and Sivers IMA Holding AB Collaborate on 5G', 'text': "NXP Semiconductors N.V. and Sivers IMA Holding AB announced a collaboration to deliver for 5G-NR (New Radio), such as gigabit Fixed Wireless Access applications. The agreement is an ecosystem relationship around NXP's highly flexible Layerscape programmable baseband platform and Sivers IMA's 5G-NR chip and phased-array antenna. Both parties will contribute to secure a high-level of integration between NXP baseband and the Sivers IMA 28 GHz and 60 GHz RFICs and phased-array antennas. Sivers IMA and NXP solution is a perfect match using Sivers IMA Zero-IF architecture that offers less current consumption and lowest cost, due to the need of fewer components. The NXP Layerscape Access portfolio of programmable baseband processors delivers unprecedented control over the 5G-NR software in order to support new O-RAN compliant options. Together with NXP Layerscape multi-core Arm SoCs and the EdgeVerse secure software framework 5G infrastructure customers can deploy a wide variety of 5GAccess Edge systems."}{'symbol': 'PYPL', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Paypal Business Loan Launches In Canada For Small Business Owners', 'text': 'PAYPAL BUSINESS LOAN LAUNCHES IN CANADA FOR SMALL BUSINESS OWNERS.'}{'symbol': 'PEP', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'PepsiCo, Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-12-2019 03:05 PM', 'text': 'PepsiCo, Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-12-2019 03:05 PM. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Marie T. Gallagher, Senior VP & Controller.'}{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'OPKO and Pfizer Announce Positive Phase 3 Top-Line Results for Somatrogon, an Investigational Long-Acting Human Growth Hormone to Treat Children with Growth Hormone Deficiency', 'text': 'OPKO Health Inc. and Pfizer Inc. announced that the global Phase 3 trial evaluating somatrogon dosed once-weekly in pre-pubertal children with growth hormone deficiency (GHD) met its primary endpoint of non-inferiority to daily GENOTROPIN® (somatropin) for injection, as measured by annual height velocity at 12 months. Top-line results from the study demonstrated that treatment with somatrogon dosed once-weekly in pre-pubertal children with GHD was non-inferior to somatropin dosed once-daily with respect to height velocity at 12 months of treatment (the primary endpoint); the least square mean was higher in the somatrogon group (10.12 cm/year) than in the somatropin group (9.78 cm/year); the treatment difference (somatrogon " somatropin) in height velocity (cm/year) was 0.33 with a two-sided 95% confidence interval of the difference of (-0.39, 1.05). In addition, change in height standard deviation scores at six and 12 months, key secondary endpoints, were higher in the somatrogon dosed once-weekly cohort in comparison to the somatropin dosed once-daily cohort.'}{'symbol': 'PPG', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'PPG Industries, Inc. Appoints Steve Pocock as Vice President, Architectural Coatings, EMEA North and East', 'text': 'PPG Industries, Inc. announced the appointment of Steve Pocock as vice president, architectural coatings, Europe, Middle East and Africa (EMEA) north and east, effective immediately. He will report to Tim Knavish, PPG executive vice president. In this expanded role, Pocock will lead PPG’s architectural coatings teams in the region, build the PPG brand assortment, drive team engagement and innovation, create increased value for customers and deliver outstanding results for shareholders.'}{'symbol': 'PLD', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Prologis, Inc. (NYSE:PLD) and Government Pension Fund Global, managed by Norges Bank Investment Management completed the acquisition of Logistics property in the London from RM Coleview 1 Ltd.', 'text': 'Prologis, Inc. (NYSE:PLD) and Government Pension Fund Global, managed by Norges Bank Investment Management agreed to acquire Logistics property in the London from RM Coleview 1 Ltd on October 21, 2019. Norges Bank Investment Management and Prologis each acquired 50% sake in this logistics property. Norges Bank Investment Management paid £35.1 million for its 50% stake.\nPrologis, Inc. (NYSE:PLD) and Government Pension Fund Global, managed by Norges Bank Investment Management completed the acquisition of Logistics property in the London from RM Coleview 1 Ltd on October 21, 2019.\n'}{'symbol': 'PVH', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tommy Hilfiger Appoints Michael Scheiner As Global Chief Marketing Officer', 'text': 'TOMMY HILFIGER APPOINTS MICHAEL SCHEINER AS GLOBAL CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER.TOMMY HILFIGER - MICHAEL SCHEINER JOINS TOMMY HILFIGER FROM HOLLISTER CO.TOMMY HILFIGER - MICHAEL WILL RELOCATE TO TOMMY HILFIGER GLOBAL HEADQUARTERS IN AMSTERDAM.'}{'symbol': 'RMD', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ResMed Introduces AirFit N30', 'text': "ResMed introduced AirFit N30, the world's first tube-down nasal cradle CPAP mask with a front-facing tube a brand-new option for sleep apnea treatment. AirFit N30 is about ease of use, helping people ease into therapy and addressing the most common pain points for longtime users."}{'symbol': 'CRM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Litify, LLC, Annual LitiQuest, Nov 07, 2019 through Nov 08, 2019', 'text': 'Litify, LLC, Annual LitiQuest, Nov 07, 2019 through Nov 08, 2019. Venue: TWA Hotel at JFK Airport, New  york, New York, United States. This two-day, free event for lawyers will provide the tools they need to revolutionize their legal marketing, improve case and reputation management, and stay ahead of the technology curve.'}{'symbol': 'SLB', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Schlumberger Limited Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 09:50 AM', 'text': 'Schlumberger Limited Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 09:50 AM. Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Apurva Mohan, IoT Security Global Lead, Principal Security Architect.'}{'symbol': 'NOW', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ServiceNow, Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 02:10 PM', 'text': 'ServiceNow, Inc. Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 02:10 PM. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Amir Jafari, VP & GM, Finance BU.'}{'symbol': 'SO', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Southern Company Announces Quarterly Dividend, Payable on December 6, 2019', 'text': "Southern Company announced a regular quarterly dividend of 62 cents per share on the company's common stock, payable December 6, 2019, to shareholders of record as of November 18, 2019."}{'symbol': 'SWK', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019', 'text': 'Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. Presents at Industrial IoT World, Oct-31-2019 . Venue: Sheraton Atlanta Hotel, 165 Courtland St NE, Atlanta, Georgia, United States. Speakers: Robert Joseph, Director, Industrial Strategy for Industry 4.0, Rodolfo Santamaria, Vice President, Global Supply Management.'}{'symbol': 'SYK', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Stryker Corporation (NYSE:SYK) completed the acquisition of Mobius Imaging, LLC and GYS Tech, LLC.', 'text': "Stryker Corporation (NYSE:SYK) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Mobius Imaging, LLC and GYS Tech, LLC for $500 million on September 4, 2019. Total consideration consists of approximately $370 million in cash upfront and up to $130 million of contingent payments associated with development and commercial milestones. The transaction is subject to customary closing conditions, including expiration of the applicable waiting period under the HSR Act and is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2019. The transaction is expected to have an immaterial impact to Stryker's net earnings in 2019. Paul Nozick of Alston & Bird LLP acted as legal advisor to Mobius. Andrew Ment, Pamela Forrest and Scott Naturman of Covington & Burling LLP acted as legal advisor to Stryker. Barclays PLC acted as financial advisor to Mobius Imaging, LLC.\nStryker Corporation (NYSE:SYK) completed the acquisition of Mobius Imaging, LLC and GYS Tech, LLC on October 21, 2019.\n"}{'symbol': 'SYY', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sysco Corporation to Report Q1, 2020 Results on Nov 04, 2019', 'text': 'Sysco Corporation announced that they will report Q1, 2020 results at 12:00 PM, GMT Standard Time on Nov 04, 2019'}{'symbol': 'TPR', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kate Spade New York Introduces Its First Sport Smartwatch', 'text': 'KATE SPADE NEW YORK INTRODUCES ITS FIRST SPORT SMARTWATCH.KATE SPADE NEW YORK - SMARTWATCHES LAUNCHES IN STORE AND ONLINE ON OCTOBER 21 AND WILL RETAIL FOR $275.'}{'symbol': 'TDY', 'date': '2019-10-21 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teledyne Awarded $178 Mln Special Operations Shallow Water Combat Submersible Contract', 'text': 'AWARDED $178 MILLION SPECIAL OPERATIONS SHALLOW WATER COMBAT SUBMERSIBLE CONTRACT.\u200dUNIT WILL CONTINUE PRODUCTION AND DELIVERY OF MK11 SWCS SYSTEMS THROUGH FISCAL YEAR 2024\u200b.'}{'symbol': 'TER', 'date': '2019-10-21 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teradyne To Acquire Autoguide Mobile Robots For $165 Million', 'text': 'TERADYNE TO ACQUIRE AUTOGUIDE MOBILE ROBOTS.TERADYNE INC - WILL ACQUIRE PRIVATELY HELD AUTOGUIDE FOR $165 MILLION.TERADYNE INC - DEAL FOR $58 MILLION NET OF CASH ACQUIRED PLUS $107 MILLION IF CERTAIN PERFORMANCE TARGETS ARE MET EXTENDING POTENTIALLY THROUGH 2022.'}{'symbol': 'TER', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teradyne, Inc. (NasdaqGS:TER) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire AutoGuide Mobile Robots for approximately $170 million.', 'text': 'Teradyne, Inc. (NasdaqGS:TER) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire AutoGuide Mobile Robots for approximately $170 million on October 18, 2019. As per the terms of the agreement, Teradyne will acquire AutoGuide Mobile Robots for $58 million net of cash and pay $107 million in earn-outs\xa0if certain performance targets are met extending potentially through 2022. AutoGuide Mobile will be included in Teradyne’s Industrial Automation segment. AutoGuide Mobile had revenues of $4 million in 2018. The transaction is subject to customary closing conditions and regulatory approval. As of November 8, 2019, the Federal Trade Commission granted early termination notice for the transaction. The acquisition is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2019. Marko Zatylny, David Saltzman, Renata Ferrari and Aaron Harsh of Ropes & Gray\xa0acted as legal advisors for Teradyne, Inc.\n'}{'symbol': 'TXT', 'date': '2019-10-21 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Textron Aviation Continues To Invest In Parts Availability, Expands Three Additional Warehouses', 'text': 'TEXTRON AVIATION CONTINUES TO INVEST IN PARTS AVAILABILITY, EXPANDS THREE ADDITIONAL WAREHOUSES.'}{'symbol': 'TMO', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Thermo Fisher Scientific Launches Cell Culture Media to Remain Stable When Stored at Room Temperature', 'text': "Thermo Fisher Scientific Inc. announced cell culture media to remain stable when stored at room temperature. Gibco BenchStable Media are the latest offering in the Gibco product line from Thermo Fisher Scientific and provide a flexible alternative for biological researchers that also saves energy. The new culture media are shipped in sustainable packaging. A 2015 study on laboratory energy consumption by the Center for Energy Efficient Laboratories determined that approximately 25% of the energy consumption in a typical lab is used for cold storage. The Gibco BenchStable Media can be stored anywhere with other temperature-stable solutions, reducing the need for cold storage. Gibco BenchStable Media are packaged in fully recyclable boxes. The packaging virtually eliminates light exposure, which can degrade basal media components and alter their performance. In addition, Gibco media bottles are made from polyethylene terephthalate with a high-density polyethylene lid, two of the most highly recycled plastics. Gibco BenchStable Media can act as a direct replacement for basal media used in researchers' existing workflows, allowing for easy substitution. The product line is available in the most commonly used basal media formulations: DMEM, DMEM/F-12, MEM, and RPMI 1640, all of which include GlutaMAX Supplement. Gibco BenchStable Media supports cellular proliferation and maximum cell densities comparable to conventional basal media formulations when supplemented with 10% Fetal Bovine Serum."}{'symbol': 'TSCO', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tractor Supply Co. to Build a New Store in Senatobia', 'text': 'Tractor Supply Co. has committed to building a new store in Senatobia. The store will be 19,000 square feet with additional space being used for outdoor displays.'}{'symbol': 'UNP', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Union Pacific Corporation Announces Offers to Exchange Certain of Its Outstanding Debt Securities for New Notes and Cash', 'text': 'Union Pacific Corporation announced the commencement of private offers to exchange certain of its outstanding notes and debentures for a combination of new notes due 2060 and cash. The outstanding notes and debentures to be exchanged pursuant to the Exchange Offers are collectively referred to as the “Existing Notes.” The Exchange Offers are being conducted upon the terms and subject to the conditions set in an offering memorandum dated October 21, 2019 and the related letter of transmittal.\xa0\xa0The Exchange Offers are only made, and copies of the offering documents will only be made available, to a holder of the Existing Notes that has certified its status as\xa0“qualified institutional buyer” as defined in Rule\xa0144A under the Securities Act of 1933 or a person who is not a “U.S. person” as defined under Regulation\xa0S under the Securities Act. Eligible Holders of Existing Notes that tender their Existing Notes prior to November 1, 2019, subject to any extension by Union Pacific (the “Early Exchange Date”), will receive an additional early exchange premium. The Exchange Offers will expire at 11:59 p.m., New York City time, on November 18, 2019, unless extended or earlier terminated by Union Pacific.\xa0\xa0Tenders of Existing Notes in the Exchange Offers may be validly withdrawn at any time prior to 5:00\xa0p.m., New York City time, on November 1, 2019, subject to extension by Union Pacific but not thereafter, except in certain limited circumstances where additional withdrawal rights are required by law. The New Notes will mature on March 20, 2060, and will bear interest at a rate per annum equal to the sum of (i) the bid-side yield on the 2.875% U.S. Treasury Note due May 15, 2049 on the Price Determination Date (based on the bid-side price indicated on the Bloomberg Screen page FIT1 at such date and time), and (ii) 1.57% (157 basis points). The New Notes have not been registered under the Securities Act or any state securities laws.\xa0\xa0Therefore, the New Notes may not be offered or sold in the United States absent registration or an applicable exemption from the registration requirements of the Securities Act and any applicable state securities laws.'}{'symbol': 'UPS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'UPS Launches New Tech-Enabled Healthcare Solutions, Standardizes Quality Systems, Forms Healthcare Unit', 'text': 'UPS announced further service enhancements for existing and new healthcare and life science customers. UPS will offer a new portfolio of tech-enabled sensing and monitoring solutions to help with the highest-quality visibility, tracking and management options for critical healthcare shipments. In addition, all UPS healthcare operations will align under a innovative, technology-driven quality management and certification system to help meet high-quality operating standards and to simplify performance verification. To accomplish this, UPS is forming a dedicated Healthcare and Life Sciences (HCLS) unit. The UPS Premier product line will provide differentiated levels of service for healthcare customers. It will leverage UPS’s Smart Global Logistics Network package tracking capabilities, combined with new, next-generation, on-package sensor technology to enable priority flow paths, sortation, contingency actions and delivery services for critical healthcare shipments. This new portfolio will provide UPS’s most comprehensive priority-handling services for chain of custody, time-dependent and temperature-sensitive packages to help increase on-time reliability. This solution is part of an expansive effort UPS is undertaking to retrofit UPS’s facility network with smart, IoT systems to track healthcare packages. These technology-enabled solutions are scheduled to come online first quarter 2020. Healthcare customers rely on best-in-class UPS quality management systems for storage, inventory management and distribution of healthcare products, particularly those which are subject to current Good Manufacturing Practices (cGMP). The UPS quality management system has been re-designed to reflect systems that exist at many pharmaceutical companies. The QMS features a cloud-based electronic document management system, global standard operating procedures (SOPs), best-in-class validation processes and global reporting tools.'}{'symbol': 'URI', 'date': '2019-10-21 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'United Rentals Announces Proposed Offering Of $750 Million Of Senior Secured Notes Due 2027', 'text': 'UNITED RENTALS ANNOUNCES PROPOSED OFFERING OF $750 MILLION OF SENIOR SECURED NOTES DUE 2027.UNITED RENTALS - INTENDS TO USE PROCEEDS FROM OFFERING, BORROWINGS TO REDEEM ALL $1 BILLION OF ITS SENIOR SECURED NOTES DUE 2023.UNITED RENTALS - AGGREGATE NET PROCEEDS FROM NOTE SALES EXPECTED TO BE ABOUT $741 MILLION AFTER UNDERWRITING DISCOUNTS, COMMISSIONS,  EXPENSES.'}{'symbol': 'UNM', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Unum Group Appoints Martha Leiper as Executive Vice President and Chief Investment Officer', 'text': 'Unum Group announced the appointment of Martha Leiper as executive vice president and chief investment officer for the company effective October 21. She is responsible for the investment and asset management strategies of Unum’s $51 billion portfolio (size excludes policy loans). Leiper previously held leadership roles of increasing responsibility with Unum from 1985-2010, most recently as senior vice president and deputy chief investment officer. Most recently, Leiper served as senior vice president, corporate finance and enterprise money movement with USAA, a diversified financial services group of companies serving people and families who serve, or served, in the United States Armed Forces. In addition to managing the USAA portfolio, she served as a senior risk officer, led an investments system modernization initiative and oversaw a variety of corporate finance functions.'}{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'EagleView to Broaden Customer Base After Court Orders Permanent Injunction Against Xactware, Verisk for Willful Infringement of Eagleview Patents', 'text': "EagleView announced that on October 18, 2019, Judge Renee Marie Bumb for the U.S. District Court of New Jersey ruled that a permanent injunction against Xactware Solutions, Inc. and Verisk Analytics, Inc. will take effect immediately to protect EagleView's proprietary intellectual property (IP) and prevent Xactware and Verisk's further willful infringement of EagleView's technology."}{'symbol': 'VZ', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verizon Communications Inc. Starts Verizon 5G Home Internet in Chicago', 'text': 'Verizon Communications Inc. announced that an internet of another kind is landing in Chicago. Starting October 24, customers in parts of the Windy City can sign up for Verizon’s 5G Home Internet - super-fast wireless broadband using the power of Verizon’s 5G Ultra Wideband Network on the 3GPP New Radio (NR) standard.'}{'symbol': 'VRTX', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated Announces FDA Approves TRIKAFTA to Treat the Underlying Cause of Cystic Fibrosis in People Ages 12 and Older Who Have at Least One F508del Mutation', 'text': 'Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated announced the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved TRIKAFTA™ (elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor and ivacaftor) for the treatment of cystic fibrosis (CF) in people ages 12 years and older who have at least one F508del mutation in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) gene, the most common CF-causing mutation. With this approval, for the first time, approximately 6,000 people with CF ages 12 years and older who have one F508del mutation and one minimal function mutation (F/MF) have a medicine that targets the underlying cause of their CF. Additionally, approximately 12,000 people with one or two F508del mutations who are currently eligible for one of Vertex’s three other FDA-approved CF medicines are now also eligible for TRIKAFTA. Vertex has submitted a Marketing Authorization Application (MAA) to the European Medicines Agency (EMA) for the elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor combination regimen. Vertex is currently evaluating elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor in people ages 6 through 11 with F/MF and F/F CF mutations in an ongoing Phase 3 study and is committed to evaluating elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor in children <6 years of age as part of planned future studies.'}{'symbol': 'VFC', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "V.F. Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019", 'text': "V.F. Corporation Presents at New Metrics '19, Nov-17-2019 through Nov-20-2019. Venue: Loews Philadelphia Hotel, Center City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-18-2019, Beth Jensen, Director of Sustainable Materials and Products. Nov-19-2019, Beth Jensen, Director of Sustainable Materials and Products."}{'symbol': 'DIS', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Walt Disney Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 through Nov-12-2019', 'text': 'The Walt Disney Company Presents at Corporate Financial Reporting Insights Conference, Nov-11-2019 through Nov-12-2019. Venue: Sheraton New York Times Square Hotel, 811 7th Avenue, W 53rd St, New york, New York, United States. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-12-2019, Brent A. Woodford, Executive Vice President of Controllership, Financial Planning & Tax.'}{'symbol': 'ZION', 'date': '2019-10-21 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Tranche Update on Zions Bancorporation, National Association (NasdaqGS:ZION)'s Equity Buyback Plan announced on August 6, 2019.", 'text': 'From July 1, 2019 to September 30, 2019, the company has repurchased 6,600,000 shares, representing 3.73% for $275 million. With this, the company has completed the repurchase of 6,600,000 shares, representing 3.73% for $275 million under the buyback announced on August 6, 2019.'}